","Here how to determine the change in equilibrium concentration of Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub><sup>4-</sup> when KCN is added to a 1.0 M Fe(HSO<sub>4</sub>)<sub>2</sub> solution.

**1. Write the Balanced Reaction**

The reaction for the formation of Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub><sup>4-</sup> is:

Fe<sup>3+</sup> (aq) + 6 KCN (aq)  ⇌  Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub><sup>4</sup> (s) + 3 K<sup>+</sup> (aq)

**2. Initial Concentrations**

*  [Fe<sup>3+</sup>]<sub>initial</sub> = 1.0 M
*  [KCN]<sub>initial</sub> =  (0.25 moles / volume)  We needs to know the volume of the solution to calculate this.  Let let volume is 0.50 L.
   [KCN]<sub>initial</sub> = 0.25 mol / 0.50 L = 050 M
*  [Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub><sup>4</sup>]<sub>initial</sub> = 0  (we negligible, as it is a very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very very  very very very very very very very  very very very very very  very very  very  very  very  very  very  very  very  very  very  very  very  very  very  very  very    very  very  very  
