The temperature is $T$.
The process is isothermal, so the temperature is constant.
The work done during an reversible process is given by
$$W = \int P dV$$
In this case, the pressure is the atmospheric pressure $P_0$ since the space above the piston is open to the atmosphere.
So, the work is
$$W = \int_{V_0}^{N \times \chi} P_0 dV = P_0 \int_{V_0}^{N \times \chi} dV = P_0 [V]_{V_0}^{N \times \chi} = P_0 (N \times \chi - V_0)$$
